= Programming with Rudiments using the unixsocketclient class =

The [../classes/html/classunixsocketclient.html unixsocketclient class] provides methods for connecting to servers over unix sockets.

Here's the code for a client that can communicate with the [unixsocketserver.html unixsocketserver program].  This client connects to a unix socket, sends a string to the server, reads what the server sends back and prints it out.

The socket filename, timeout, retry wait, and number of tries are all configurable.

{{{#!blockquote
{{{#!code
@../../examples/unixsocketclient.cpp@
}}}
}}}

Unix sockets allow clients and servers on the same machine to communicate.  See the [inetsocketserver.html inetsocketserver] and [inetsocketclient.html inetsocketclient] examples for clients and servers that can communcate across a network.

